  "markdown": "Where we work\n\n# Wallpaper installation in Kensington\n\nTownhouses, mansion flats and family houses in Kensington and Holland Park. Surveying, supply, installation and aftercare from one London practice.\n\n[Start your project](https://www.mrwallcover.com/contact/) [See the work](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/)\n\nKensington houses range from Victorian stucco to later mansion blocks, and the walls vary as much as the architecture. The survey is a judgement on the wall as well as a measure of it. If the wall is not ready for the material specified, we say so before the last drop is ordered.\n\nWe hang silk, grasscloth and other natural weaves, fabric walling, vinyl, hand-painted papers in the manner of de Gournay and Fromental, murals and acoustic wallcoverings. Paper can be hung to joinery where the drawings show it.\n\nPrivate clients are not named. Residential work appears only by street or area, with the homeowner's agreement. The public record of our work is on the projects page; Kensington homes appear in its [fuller project record](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/#project-record), by area only.\n\n![Cadence Oxblood behind BEVERLY 1975's tables during Brompton Design District.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/beverly-08-800.webp)\n\nOur work in South Kensington: Calico Wallpaper Cadence behind BEVERLY 1975's tables at [The Lavery, Cromwell Place](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/calico-beverly-1975-cadence/), during Brompton Design District. Photograph: Dorin Burcus / Mr Wallcover.\n\n## On the public record\n\n[![Cadence Oxblood behind BEVERLY 1975's tables during Brompton Design District.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/beverly-08-800.webp)](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/calico-beverly-1975-cadence/)\n\nCadence Oxblood behind BEVERLY 1975's tables during Brompton Design District. Photograph: Dorin Burcus / Mr Wallcover.\n\n### [Calico Wallpaper x BEVERLY 1975: Cadence at The Lavery, Brompton Design District](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/calico-beverly-1975-cadence/)\n\nWallcovering installation (feature wall), 2026.\n\n[View the project](https://www.mrwallcover.com/projects/calico-beverly-1975-cadence/)\n\nQuestions\n\n## Questions about papering in Kensington\n\nIllustrative material studies\n\nPause motion\n\n### Which wallcoverings do you hang in Kensington homes?\n\nSilk, grasscloth and natural weaves, fabric walling, vinyl and contract wallcoverings, hand-painted papers, murals, and acoustic wallcoverings and panels.\n\n### How much extra wallpaper should I order?\n\nEnough to cover the pattern repeat and the wastage it creates. That allowance is typically 15–30%, depending on the pattern repeat and the layout, with staircases at the high end (around 30%) because of the angles.\n\n## What happens next\n\n1. Dorin Burcus reads your note.\n2. You can book a 20-minute call to talk the project through.\n3. If the project needs a survey, we arrange it after we have spoken.\n4. After the survey we write a scope of works by room.\n\n[Start your project](https://www.mrwallcover.com/contact/)\n\nBy [Dorin Burcus](https://www.mrwallcover.com/about/#dorin), founder · Last reviewed 9 October 2026\n",
